{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggt4XGSDhR1QGXuzNUJX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Setup.** Tetrahedral d⁸ behaves like octahedral d² with the sign of Dq reversed. The ground state is ³T₁(F). The first excited triplet, ³T₂, is not mixed with any other term of the same symmetry. Its energy above the ground state is exactly 8Dq.\n\n**Dq.** The ³T₂ band is at 4 400 cm⁻¹, so 8Dq = 4 400 and Dq ≈ 550 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B.** The ³T₁(F) and ³T₁(P) terms mix. Their 2×2 matrix is:\n\n- ³T₁(F) diagonal element: −6Dq\n- ³T₁(P) diagonal element: 15B\n- off-diagonal element: 6B\n\nThe separation of the two roots is therefore\n\nΔE = √[(15B + 6Dq)² + 4(6B)²] = √[(15B + 6Dq)² + 144B²]\n\nSet ΔE = 15 500 cm⁻¹ and 6Dq = 3 300 cm⁻¹:\n\n(15B + 3300)² + 144B² = 15500²\n\nThis simplifies to 369B² + 99 000B − 2.294×10⁸ = 0.\n\nThe positive root is B ≈ 666 cm⁻¹.\n\n**C.** The assumed ratio C/B = 4.5 gives C ≈ 3 000 cm⁻¹. C affects only the spin-flip singlet states, so it does not enter the triplet fit.\n\n**Result:** Dq ≈ 550 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 666 cm⁻¹. This B is about 0.64 of the free-ion value of roughly 1 040 cm⁻¹, which is chemically reasonable.\n\n{\"Dq\": 550, \"B\": 666, \"C\": 2997, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"3T2 = 8Dq gives Dq; the 3T1(F)-3T1(P) 2x2 matrix fitted to 15500 cm-1 gives B.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":845,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef0f4323-33f9-409d-a31a-1e26bf339471","uuid":"74e713fb-be5e-4059-8b50-cb68454ae233","timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:42:59.878Z","request_id":"req_011Cggt4Wv6aQKkspSuEbLWs"}
